{
  "_note": [
    "6E Standard (400) complication packages. AUTHORED — the 5E packages are sized to 100, which is",
    "5E LOW POWERED's disadvantage limit. 6E Standard's complication limit is 75.",
    "",
    "Complications are taken at the FIXED limit, so each package must total exactly 75. Nothing here",
    "declares a cost: every complication is priced from its adders by the engine.",
    "",
    "NO NORMAL CHARACTERISTIC MAXIMA. Three of the four 5E packages carry NCM at a flat 20 — a fifth",
    "of the whole limit — and 6E ABOLISHED it. There are no characteristic maxima in 6E, so there is",
    "nothing to take a complication for. It is also the one entry in the 5E data with a hardcoded",
    "basecost rather than a template, which is how it got away with it.",
    "",
    "So a 6E package is 75 points of real complications where a 5E one was 80 plus a 20-point",
    "bookkeeping entry. Less room, and all of it has to mean something at the table."
  ],
